rule section_34_1 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1:
a legal practitioner must not accept the EA an executive appointment under section_34_1 if
    the executive appointment is an executive appointment
    and a business is a business
    and the legal practitioner is a legal practitioner
    and the EA the executive appointment is associated with the business
    and the business is described in section 1.

% What section 34(1) concludes holds.
rule section_34_1_conclusion with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1:
a legal practitioner must not accept the EA an executive appointment if
    the legal practitioner must not accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_1.

rule section_34_1_a with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 a:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is a business
    and the business detracts from the dignity of the legal profession.

rule section_34_1_a_2 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 a:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is a business
    and the business is incompatible with the dignity of the legal profession.

rule section_34_1_a_3 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 a:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is a business
    and the business derogates from the dignity of the legal profession.

rule section_34_1_b with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 b:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is described in section 1 under section_34_1_b_i.

rule section_34_1_b_2 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 b:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is described in section 1 under section_34_1_b_ii.

rule section_34_1_b_3 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 b:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is described in section 1 under section_34_1_b_iii.

practicing_as_a_lawyer is an occupation, as stated in the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 b i.

rule section_34_1_b_i with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 b i:
a business is described in section 1 under section_34_1_b_i if
    the business is a business
    and a legal practitioner is a legal practitioner
    and the primary occupation of the legal practitioner is practicing_as_a_lawyer
    and the business materially interferes with the primary occupation of the legal practitioner.

% What section 34(1)(b)(i) concludes holds.
rule section_34_1_b_i_conclusion with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 b i:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is described in section 1 under section_34_1_b_i.

rule section_34_1_b_ii with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 b ii:
a business is described in section 1 under section_34_1_b_ii if
    the business is a business
    and a legal practitioner is a legal practitioner
    and the business materially interferes with the availability to practice law of the legal practitioner.

% What section 34(1)(b)(ii) concludes holds.
rule section_34_1_b_ii_conclusion with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 b ii:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is described in section 1 under section_34_1_b_ii.

rule section_34_1_e with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 e:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is a business
    and the business is described in the first schedule.

rule section_34_1_f with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 f:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is a business
    and the business is prohibited.

rule section_34_1_c with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 c:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is a business
    and the business is likely to unfairly attract business.

rule section_34_1_b_iii with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 b iii:
a business is described in section 1 under section_34_1_b_iii if
    the business is a business
    and a legal practitioner is a legal practitioner
    and the business materially interferes with the representation of their clients of the legal practitioner.

% What section 34(1)(b)(iii) concludes holds.
rule section_34_1_b_iii_conclusion with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 b iii:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is described in section 1 under section_34_1_b_iii.

sharing is a payment type, as stated in the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 d.

paying is a payment type, as stated in the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 d.

fees is a compensation type, as stated in the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 d.

commission is a compensation type, as stated in the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 d.

rule section_34_1_d with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 d:
a person is a person if
    the person is a legal practitioner.

rule section_34_1_d_2 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 d:
a payment reason is a payment reason if
    the payment reason is legal work.

rule section_34_1_d_3 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 d:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is a business
    and a payment is a payment
    and the business involves the payment
    and a person is the recipient of the payment
    and the person is authorized to provide legal services
    and the payment is for a payment reason
    and the payment reason is legal work
    and the payment reason was done by a second person
    and the second person is a legal practitioner
    and the payment is of payment type sharing
    and the payment has fees.

rule section_34_1_d_4 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 1 d:
a business is described in section 1 if
    the business is a business
    and a payment is a payment
    and the business involves the payment
    and a person is the recipient of the payment
    and the person is authorized to provide legal services
    and the payment is for a payment reason
    and the payment reason is legal work
    and the payment reason was done by a second person
    and the second person is a legal practitioner
    and the payment is of payment type paying
    and the payment has commission.

rule section_34_3 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 3:
a legal practitioner may accept the EA an executive appointment under section_34_3 if
    the legal practitioner is a legal practitioner
    and the executive appointment is an executive appointment
    and a business entity is a business entity
    and a service is a service
    and the executive appointment is an executive appointment in the business entity
    and the business entity provides the service
    and the service is a law related service
    and it is not the case that the legal practitioner must not accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_1.

% What section 34(3) concludes holds.
rule section_34_3_conclusion with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 3:
a legal practitioner may accept the EA an executive appointment if
    the legal practitioner may accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_3.

rule section_34_3_2 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 3:
an executive appointment is an executive appointment in a business entity if
    the executive appointment is an executive appointment
    and the business entity is a business entity
    and the executive appointment is in the business entity.

rule section_34_2 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 2:
a legal practitioner may accept the EA an executive appointment under section_34_2 if
    the legal practitioner is a legal practitioner
    and a thing is a singapore law practice
    and the executive appointment is an executive appointment
    and a second thing is a singapore law practice
    and the legal practitioner is a legal practitioner in the thing
    and the executive appointment is an executive appointment in the second thing
    and every owner of the second thing is sole prop, partner, or director of the thing
    and it is not the case that the legal practitioner must not accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_1.

% What section 34(2) concludes holds.
rule section_34_2_conclusion with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 2:
a legal practitioner may accept the EA an executive appointment if
    the legal practitioner may accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_2.

rule section_34_2_2 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 2:
a legal practitioner may accept the EA an executive appointment under section_34_2 if
    the legal practitioner is a legal practitioner
    and a thing is a singapore law practice
    and the executive appointment is an executive appointment
    and a second thing is a singapore law practice
    and the legal practitioner is a legal practitioner in the thing
    and the executive appointment is an executive appointment in the second thing
    and the legal practitioner accepts the executive appointment as a representative
    and it is not the case that it is prohibited for the thing to be involved in the second thing
    and it is not the case that the legal practitioner must not accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_1.

global is a globe, as stated in the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 4.

