singapore is a jurisdiction, as stated in the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 6 a.

rule section_34_6_a with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 6 a:
a legal practitioner must not accept the EA an executive appointment if
    the legal practitioner is a legal practitioner
    and the executive appointment is an executive appointment
    and a law practice is a law practice
    and the legal practitioner is a legal practitioner in the law practice
    and the law practice is located in singapore
    and a second law practice is a law practice
    and the second law practice is located in singapore
    and the executive appointment is an executive appointment in law practice the second law practice
    and all of
        it is not the case that the legal practitioner may accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_2
        and it is not the case that the legal practitioner may accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_3
        and it is not the case that the legal practitioner may accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_4
        and it is not the case that the legal practitioner may accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_5.

rule section_34_6_b with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 6 b:
a legal practitioner must not accept the EA an executive appointment if
    the legal practitioner is a legal practitioner
    and the executive appointment is an executive appointment
    and a business entity is a business entity
    and the executive appointment is an executive appointment in the business entity
    and all of
        it is not the case that the legal practitioner may accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_2
        and it is not the case that the legal practitioner may accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_3
        and it is not the case that the legal practitioner may accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_4
        and it is not the case that the legal practitioner may accept the EA the executive appointment under section_34_5.

rule section_34_9_c with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 9 c:
an executive appointment is an executive appointment if
    the executive appointment is a category name
    and the executive appointment entitles the holder to executive authority
    and it is not the case that the executive appointment is an executive directorship
    and it is not the case that the executive appointment is an independent directorship
    and a business is a business
    and the executive appointment is associated with the business.

rule section_34_9_c_2 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 9 c:
an executive appointment is an executive appointment if
    the executive appointment is a category name
    and the executive appointment entitles the holder to executive authority
    and it is not the case that the executive appointment is an executive directorship
    and it is not the case that the executive appointment is an independent directorship
    and a business entity is a business entity
    and the executive appointment is in the business entity.

rule section_34_9_c_3 with provenance the Legal Profession Professional Conduct Rules at section 34 9 c:
an executive appointment is an executive appointment if
    the executive appointment is a category name
    and the executive appointment entitles the holder to executive authority
    and it is not the case that the executive appointment is an executive directorship
    and it is not the case that the executive appointment is an independent directorship
    and a law practice is a law practice
    and the executive appointment is in the law practice the law practice.

